Two Codex settings, each of which clew calls harmless on its own.

`approval_policy = "never"` is not a finding because the sandbox still bounds
what an unasked agent reaches. `sandbox_mode = "workspace-write"` is not a
finding because something still asks. Set together they leave neither
control, and what the agent may write unasked includes the files deciding
what the next run does.

>>> .codex/config.toml
approval_policy = "never"
sandbox_mode = "workspace-write"
